# Death-penalty experience recovery through the 1.2 priest prayer (skill 17063).
#
# The victim (GM) reaches level 21 and adds 5 000 exp, so the next death loses the 5 % of the
# level span into `recoverable_exp` (80 % recoverable). The caster (GM) kills it. The victim
# revives with `/revive` (the GM revive keeps the recoverable exp) and casts 17063 the way the
# 1.2 priest window does (`X2Priest:RecoverExp` -> `CSStartSkill`, caster and target self; the
# skill resolves its self target back to the caster and still needs a priest within 10 m, the
# temple priest 502 at the Solzreed start). The recovery must answer with
# `SCRecoverableExpPacket` (zero left), `SCCharacterLaborPowerChangedPacket` (level 21 labor)
# and `SCExpChangedPacket`; the pre-#21 `NO_PERM` refusal would leave the exp lost.
#
# `rawcs` is used instead of `cast` because `cast` drains for up to 8 s and would swallow the
# 6.5 s prayer's effect packets, which are what this suite asserts.

suite exp-recovery
bot victim gm
bot caster gm

[caster]
gm level 21
waitpeer 120 ${victim}
sync ready 2
pkill ${victim}
sync dead 2

[victim]
gm level 21
gm xp 5000
gm labor 100
sync ready 2
sync dead 2
gm revive
pump 1
# CSStartSkill: skill 17063, Unit caster (self), Unit target (self), no skill object.
rawcs 052 a742000000SELF000000SELF00
# The effect sends the labor change first, then SCRecoverableExpPacket, then the exp delta.
expectpkt SCCharacterLaborPowerChangedPacket 12
expectpkt SCRecoverableExpPacket 5
expectpkt SCExpChangedPacket 5
